<title>JAPAN: Test Testing reveals problem loans.</title>
<headline>Test Testing reveals problem loans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Test Test Co Ltd KK has disclosed its restructured loans (in billions of yen unless specified):</p>
<p>					end-Sep 96     end-Mar 96</p>
<p>  Restructured loans		0.1		0.1</p>
<p>  Bad loans			   0.2		0.1</p>
<p>  Non-performing loans	    0.4		0.2</p>
<p>  Loans to troubled clients     0.1		0.1</p>
<p>  Total problem loans	     0.8		0.5</p>
<p>Restructured loans are those on which interest rates have been cut to help corporate restructuring. Bad loans are to bankrupt firms and non-performing are those with interest payments in arrears by six months or more. Loans to troubled clients are mainly to the bank's non-bank affiliates.</p>
</text>
